    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d285">

                <pb facs="0563" n="493" sameAs="frus:frus1883/pg493"/>

                <head>No. 285.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Frelinghuysen to Mr. West.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1883-02-03"><hi rendition="#italic">February</hi> 3,
                        1883</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to my note to you of the 17th
                    ultimo, in relation to the transit of Chinese laborers through the territory of
                    the United States when passing to or from a third country, I have now the honor
                        <pb facs="0564" n="494" xml:id="pg494"/> to transmit for your information
                    four copies of a recent circular<anchor n="*" xml:id="d285-f1"/> issued by the
                    Secretary of the Treasury, in which are set forth the conditions under which
                    such transit may be accomplished.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>FRED’K T. FRELINGHUYSEN.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
